// title: Windows Network Sniffing · Sentinel
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Defender for Endpoint
// tables: DeviceProcessEvents
// purpose: In Windows the default tool Packet Monitor can be used to capture network traffic. This traffic might contain valueble information that an attacker can use. Valueble information can be found in HTTP traffic, because it goes unencrypted over the wire.
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/Defender%20For%20Endpoint/WindowsNetworkSniffing.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName == "PktMon.exe"
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, ProcessCommandLine
